00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
A four-stroke spark-ignition teaching model orders intake, compression, power and exhaust across two crankshaft turns. Real valve events overlap.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
One ideal cycle = 2 × 360° = 720° of crank rotation.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
Sequence the 720° cycle

01:00.000 --> 01:12.000
This ideal mechanism leaves out friction, temperature and part-specific behavior. Real designs need measurements.

